From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:52:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] replica-age resume: pin future seen_at, the
 memo-only detach and seen_at = last observation

Post-merge check t_01a1d61df02c9eca of #2477 found three mutants of
hermes_cli/kanban_sync_replica_age.py that survive the suite. Test-only change:

- A1 (_resume `since <= seen_at <= now` -> `since <= seen_at`): a this-boot
  record whose seen_at is 60 s in the future now starts the clock afresh; the
  same record seen 60 s ago resumes (30 awake min old, files one card).
- A3 (_check_board `known is not None or slug in _load_memo()` ->
  `known is not None`): after a restart (empty _SEEN) a detach drops the
  board's record from .replica-age.json, and a re-attach does not resume the
  old clock (no card 22 min after the first check, 6 after re-attach).
- A4 (_remember `"seen_at": now` -> `"seen_at": seen.since`): a 64-min stall
  with a restart every 4 min keeps seen_at at the last observation, one card
  at 08:20 PT and the original since with the incident still open.

RED/GREEN (hermes-core-wt test tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_sync_replica_age.py):
main + new tests: 30 passed. A1: 1 failed (future[60.0-False]); A3: 1 failed
(detached_after_a_restart...); A4: 1 failed (an_hour_long_stall...).

